## UNIVERSAL RULES

1. **EDWOSB box ALWAYS stays gold/amber** — `#fef3c7` / `#fde68a` / `#d97706` — never changes regardless of service lane
2. **Match the color to the SERVICE being offered**, not the buyer's agency (unless state override applies)
3. **Apply colors to:** header gradient, section headers, title bar, border-left accents, NAICS tags, checkmark icons, highlight boxes
4. **Logo section background stays WHITE** — always `#ffffff` so the DDI logo displays cleanly
5. **Text on colored backgrounds stays WHITE** — headers, section titles, badges
6. **If a cap statement covers MULTIPLE services** — use the PRIMARY service lane's color (the one most relevant to what the buyer is buying)
7. **When in doubt** — ask which service lane is primary, don't guess

